ed and compositions of imaged surfaces to be inferred. Daytime infrared Themis images typically emphasize topography, with warmer sunward slopes being brighter than cooler shaded slopes. Nighttime Themis images emphasize differences in thermal inertia between areas being observed, giving insights into the physical characteristics of the surfaces. This map is a THEMIS nighttime infrared map. The 2017 release featured preliminary geodetically controlled mosaics tied to a known coordinate system (USGS Viking Orbiter MDIM 2.1), spatially adjusted to align feature boundaries, and orthoprojected at 100 m/pixel scale. Further adjustments have been processed for the 2018 release of this final mosaic.", "catalog_uuid": "ecbd1840-2302-49c8-be40-86740c21ea98", "declared_crs": "urn:ogc:def:crs:EPSG::104905", "product_created_at": "2020-06-25T22:48:19Z"}}	01030000208C7E0E00010000000500000050F05EFFFF7F66C09B9F2CC60A4050C075289E0EFF7F66409B9F2CC60A4050C075289E0EFF7F6640E27668580C40504050F05EFFFF7F66C0E27668580C40504050F05EFFFF7F66C09B9F2CC60A4050C0
