demo_delta_scarp_sample	demo_jezero_planning_context	DEMONSTRATION: Delta scarp sample site	geology	Синтетическая точка у обрыва дельты. DEMONSTRATION DATA.	01010000208C7E0E003D0AD7A3705D5340B81E85EB51783240	\N	\N	DEMONSTRATION DATA	t
sci_delta_hawksbill	m2020_rover_waypoints	Delta front (Hawksbill Gap / Wildcat Ridge)	sedimentary_formations	Fine-grained laminated mudstones and sandstones at the eroded front of Jezero's western fan. Interpreted as ancient delta-front lake deposits capable of preserving fine mineral textures; contains sulfate-bearing layers, not verified as evidence of life.	01010000208C7E0E002E73BA2C265A5340855FEAE74D753240	-2526.5	536	26_2018	f
sci_crism_clays_fan	mro_crism_hyd_jezero	Jezero fan Fe/Mg phyllosilicate unit	clay_minerals	Orbital infrared spectral summary signature (BD1900_2 / BD2100_2) consistent with hydrated Fe/Mg phyllosilicates. Orbital detection is a candidate mineral indicator and requires in-situ rover spectroscopy to confirm mineralogy.	01010000208C7E0E006891ED7C3F5953402DB29DEFA7763240	-2498	\N	FRT00005C5E_PHY	f
sci_margin_carbonates	m2020_rover_waypoints	Margin Unit carbonate belt	carbonate_deposits	Direct rover detection of Mg/Fe carbonate-rich outcrops along the inner western margin of Jezero Crater. One working hypothesis links the belt to shoreline precipitation or low-temperature aqueous alteration.	01010000208C7E0E00D105F52D7356534008944DB9C27B3240	-2423.5	911	44_4982	f
sci_neretva_fluvial	usgs_iau_mars_nomenclature	Neretva Vallis inlet & Bright Angel margin	ancient_fluvial	Incised breach channel cutting Jezero's western rim, interpreted from orbital morphology and strata as the ancient fluvial inlet that fed water and sediment into the crater basin.	01010000208C7E0E000B98C0ADBB535340ADFA5C6DC57E3240	-2361.3	1171	52_6980	f
sci_seitah_outcrop	m2020_rover_waypoints	Séítah olivine-bearing outcrop (Bastide)	rock_outcrops	Directly measured coarse olivine cumulate bedrock showing carbonate and sulfate alteration along crystal rims, indicating post-emplacement interaction with liquid water.	01010000208C7E0E00952BBCCB455C5340825660C8EA6E3240	-2575.2	202	7_1556	f
sci_belva_layers	m2020_rover_waypoints	Belva crater stratigraphic wall	geological_layers	900 m impact crater excavating dipping stratified beds of the upper Jezero delta, exposing cross-bedded sandstones and boulder-rich layers in direct Mastcam-Z panoramas.	01010000208C7E0E00C49448A2975753404FCC7A31947B3240	-2421.6	784	39_926	f
sci_three_forks_depot	m2020_rover_waypoints	Three Forks sample cache & water-altered regolith	potential_water_features	Ten sealed titanium sample tubes deposited on the crater floor containing igneous and water-altered sedimentary cores archived for laboratory return. Samples preserve geologic context, not confirmed biosignatures.	01010000208C7E0E0092B3B0A71D5A53405DE15D2EE2733240	-2545.3	658	32_378	f
sci_butler_contact	m2020_rover_waypoints	Octavia E. Butler crater-floor geological contact	geological_contacts	Boundary region between fractured crater-floor igneous units (Máaz formation) and eroded remnants of the fan apron. Relative age relationships between floor units remain a scientific hypothesis refined by core dating.	01010000208C7E0E006688635DDC5C53408BC3995FCD713240	-2569.9	14	3_110	f
